        "original_id": "1ef3b5d0-d4e8-5757-bfa6-7bb2975fb6e9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Don Chafin\n- Places: Logan County, West Virginia; southwestern West Virginia coalfields\n- Events: Battle of Blair Mountain\n- Roles: sheriff; commander\n- Organizations: Logan Defenders\n- Topics: coal miners' unionization\n\nFacts:\n- Don Chafin was born on June 26, 1887.\n- In late August and early September 1921, the Battle of Blair Mountain lasted five days in Logan County, West Virginia.\n- In the Battle of Blair Mountain, about 10,000 armed coal miners confronted 3,000 lawmen and strikebreakers called the Logan Defenders.\n- The Logan Defenders were backed by coal mine operators during the miners' attempt to unionize the southwestern West Virginia coalfields.\n- Don Chafin was the sheriff of Logan County, West Virginia, and a commander in the Battle of Blair Mountain.\n- Don Chafin died on August 9, 1954.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
